Topic: GIS  
Content: There was no coding involved in the GIS workshop; it was instead just about adding layers based on data points, ranging from river outlines, mapping outlining, clipping, and overlapping, with its general notes held in the log file.
Also, due to the different machine, no files were saved, and instead an image of the Ontario outline along with the rivers is in the image folder. For the gravestone, many of the areas seemed unclear on how the designation should be done with 
things like culture, and certain tombstone labelling being too restrictive. For example, my partner Nick and I for the taskof classifying the top of the gravestone were unable to reach a consensus on the type of headstone due to some damage being present


