Overall, the LiDAR was not effective at detecting fine details during scanning. However, the grave was slightly visible in terms of shape during the
first scan, with the time spent scanning around not appearing to have additional impact for the few moments. I was unable to use the more in 
depth laser scanner on the gravestone shards, but the results were influenced by light, with a darker area providing clearer readings.

The measurements couldn't be done, but it seemed to follow the process of using a compass to establish a direction for mapping purposes and using the angle from that direction to plot distance to points of interest.


